[center][size=6][color=#42FA60][b]FO4 Community Shaders[/b][/color][/size]
[b]Modern rendering for Fallout 4.[/b]
[color=#A8B5A8]Configured through Dear Modding UI[/color][/center]

[b]FO4 Community Shaders[/b] brings modern lighting, shadows, reflections, water, and upscaling to Fallout 4 as a single F4SE plugin. It is a port of [url=https://github.com/community-shaders/skyrim-community-shaders]Skyrim Community Shaders[/url], rebuilt on the game's own renderer. Every feature ships turned off, so you enable only what you want.

[color=#FFB84D][b]⚠ Beta:[/b] Features are still being developed and tested. Please report what you find.[/color]

[size=5][color=#42FA60][b]✦ FEATURES[/b][/color][/size]
[b]● Lighting[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Screen Space GI:[/b] Ambient occlusion and indirect lighting.[/*]
[*][b]Skylighting:[/b] Ambient light and reflections that respect how much sky a surface can see.[/*]
[*][b]Image Based Lighting:[/b] Ambient light, reflections, and fog tint from the sky and environment. Requires Dynamic Cubemaps.[/*]
[*][b]Light Limit Fix:[/b] Effects and water receive every nearby light, with inverse-square falloff for lights authored in Lights TOML files.[/*]
[*][b]Screen Space Shadows:[/b] Contact shadows and finer shadow detail.[/*]
[*][b]Sky Sync[/b] [color=#42FA60]NEW[/color][b]:[/b] Sun, moon and godrays follow the bodies in the sky.[/*]
[*][b]Volumetric Shadows[/b] [color=#42FA60]NEW[/color][b]:[/b] Softer sun rim and back lighting, and sun shadows on water and effects.[/*]
[*][b]Cloud Shadows[/b] [color=#42FA60]NEW[/color][b]:[/b] Moving clouds shade the landscape and water.[/*]
[/list]
[b]● Materials[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Subsurface Scattering[/b] [color=#42FA60]NEW[/color][b]:[/b] Realistic skin scattering, replacing the vanilla skin blur.[/*]
[*][b]Dynamic Cubemaps:[/b] Reflections that respond to the surrounding scene.[/*]
[*][b]Extended Materials:[/b] Parallax on objects and terrain, with sun self-shadows.[/*]
[/list]
[b]● Landscape & Water[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Terrain Shadows:[/b] Long-range shadows cast by distant terrain.[/*]
[*][b]Terrain Blending[/b] [color=#42FA60]NEW[/color][b]:[/b] Terrain blends into objects that sink into it.[/*]
[*][b]Terrain Variation:[/b] Breaks up repeating terrain textures, including distant LOD.[/*]
[*][b]LOD Blending:[/b] Matches distant terrain and object brightness to nearby areas.[/*]
[*][b]Water Effects:[/b] Water parallax and sunlight caustics.[/*]
[*][b]Unified Water:[/b] Distant water that matches nearby water.[/*]
[/list]
[b]● Display & Utility[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Upscaling:[/b] TAA, FSR 3/4, and DLSS, with NVIDIA Reflex or experimental AMD Anti-Lag 2.[/*]
[*][b]Frame Generation:[/b] FSR 3/4 and DLSS, including Multi Frame Generation.[/*]
[*][b]Motion Vector Fixes, Performance Overlay, CS Editor:[/b] Motion-data fixes, frame and GPU timing graphs, and weather and time controls.[/*]
[/list]

[size=5][color=#42FA60][b]✦ INSTALLATION[/b][/color][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Required:[/b] Fallout 4 [b]1.11.240[/b], [url=https://f4se.silverlock.org/]F4SE[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/47327]Address Library[/url].[/*]
[*][b]Recommended:[/b] [url=https://github.com/Dear-Modding-FO4/DearModdingUI]Dear Modding UI[/url] 2.2+ for the in-game menu, [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/84214]Addictol[/url] for engine fixes.[/*]
[*][b]GPU:[/b] Upscaling and frame generation need DX12; DLSS needs NVIDIA RTX, FSR 4 a compatible Radeon.[/*]
[/list]
Install with your mod manager, launch through F4SE, open Community Shaders in Dear Modding UI, enable the features you want, and restart the game.

[b]✗ Remove[/b] standalone [b]Motion Vector Fixes[/b] and [b]Dynamic Cubemaps F4[/b]; Community Shaders includes both and disables itself while they are installed.

[size=5][color=#42FA60][b]✦ FAQ[/b][/color][/size]
[b]Is this mod compatible with ENB?[/b]
I will now have to publicly execute you.

[b]I installed it and nothing changed.[/b]
Every feature ships turned off. Enable them in Dear Modding UI, then restart.

[b]Why is the first launch slow?[/b]
Shaders compile once and are cached; the main menu holds loading until they finish. To play while they compile, set [b]background_compilation = true[/b] under [b][shader_cache][/b] in FO4CommunityShaders.toml.

[b]DLSS/FSR or frame generation won't turn on.[/b]
Use borderless windowed mode; exclusive fullscreen falls back to TAA.

[b]HDR and ReShade?[/b]
Windows Auto HDR, RTX HDR and ReShade (dxgi.dll) work. RenoDX and Special K HDR do not work with Upscaling or Frame Generation.

[b]Linux / Steam Deck?[/b]
Place a Windows 10 [b]d3dcompiler_47.dll[/b] next to Fallout4.exe; Proton's own compiler cannot build the shaders.

[b]Safe to add or remove mid-playthrough?[/b]
Yes. It has no plugin file and writes nothing to your saves.

[size=5][color=#42FA60][b]✦ LINKS & SUPPORT[/b][/color][/size]
[url=https://github.com/northaxosky/fallout4-community-shaders][b]GitHub[/b][/url] ● [url=https://github.com/northaxosky/fallout4-community-shaders/issues/new/choose][b]Report an Issue[/b][/url] ● [url=https://github.com/northaxosky/fallout4-community-shaders/releases][b]Development Builds[/b][/url] ● [url=https://discord.com/invite/nkrQybAsyy][b]Discord[/b][/url] ([url=https://discord.com/channels/1080142797870485606/1553853859972124712]Fallout 4 channel[/url])

When reporting a problem, attach [b]FO4CommunityShaders.log[/b] (in [b]Documents\My Games\Fallout4\F4SE\[/b]) and [b]FO4CommunityShaders.toml[/b] (in [b]Data\F4SE\Plugins\FO4CommunityShaders\[/b], or MO2's Overwrite), and list your GPU and enabled features.

